Not surprising that you got that kind of an error message. The game had
crashed because the disk got full, which means it didn't have enough space
to write what it wanted, so some level file got truncated. This happens
when you're changing dungeon levels or save the game, because that's when
the game writes level information to the disk.  
And when one of the level files is not intact, it is quite logical that
the recovered saved file isn't intact either.

